<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>ax12_arm</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
  <author>
    <name>Jupiter Robot</name>
    <email>support@jupiterobot.com</email>
  </author>
  <description>
    Legacy AX-12 arm meshes.

    The RoboCup world files (robocup_2024.world.xml, robocup_2025.world.xml)
    contain baked-in SDF for a robot that still had the AX-12 arm, and they
    reference model://jupiterobot2_arm_description/meshes/*.stl.

    jupiterobot2_arm_description was deleted when the SO-100 was fitted, so
    those URIs would fail to resolve and Gazebo would spawn the robocup worlds
    with invisible arm geometry. Rather than keep a whole dead ROS package
    around for seven STL files, the meshes live here and the world files point
    at model://ax12_arm/meshes/*.stl.

    This is asset-only. Nothing in this package describes the current robot;
    the live arm is SO-100 (so100_description).
  </description>
</model>
